{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.AddableCellIndexing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.AddableCellIndexing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.BranchingGenericity","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramCornerReindex"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_addable_wenzlWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_addable_wenzlWeight","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AddableCellIndexing.lean#L88-L145","doc":"**Branching over the addable cells.**\n\n`∑_{s addable to μ} w_{μ+s} = w_μ`.\n\nSame content as `sum_wenzlWeight_addCellOrSelf`, in the indexing\n`YoungDiagramCornerReindex.sum_corner_eq_sum_addable` produces — which is what the normalisation\ninduction consumes.\n\nThe two row ranges are reconciled by cases, and **both directions carry a real fact**:\n\n* `colLen 0 < r` — rows `colLen 0 < a < r` are empty and so is the row above them, so\n  `isAddableCell_rowEnd_iff` refuses them and the guard is `0`;\n* `colLen 0 = r` — row `r` *is* addable, and its term vanishes only because the resulting diagram\n  has `r+1` rows (`wenzlWeight_addCell_beyond_eq_zero`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_addable_eq_sum_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_addable_eq_sum_range","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AddableCellIndexing.lean#L74-L82","doc":"**The addable-cell subtype sum is the guarded row sum.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.mem_addableRowSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.mem_addableRowSet","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AddableCellIndexing.lean#L60-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.addableRowSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.addableRowSet","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AddableCellIndexing.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The addable cells of `μ`, as an explicit `Finset`: one per row `a ≤ colLen 0` that admits a box,\nsitting at `(a, μ_a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.isCornerCell_row_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.isCornerCell_row_lt","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AddableCellIndexing.lean#L46-L52","doc":"**A corner cell sits strictly inside the column height.**  The corner analogue of\n`isAddableCell_row_le`: a corner is a *cell of* `ν`, so its row is occupied, hence `< colLen 0`.\n(The addable bound is `≤`, not `<`, because an addable cell may start a brand-new row.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.isAddableCell_row_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.isAddableCell_row_le","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AddableCellIndexing.lean#L35-L44","doc":"An addable cell sits in row `≤ colLen 0`: either it is in row `0`, or the cell above it is in\n`μ`, which bounds its row by the column height. ","signatureChunk":0}]}